Project: Ayana, a spiritual travel marketplace.
- client/: React 19 + Vite + React Three Fiber. Plain CSS in src/styles.css. All API calls go through src/api.js.
- api/: Python FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2 + Alembic + Pydantic, MySQL. Routes in app/routers, business rules in app/services,
  tables in app/models.py, request shapes in app/schemas.py, JSON shapes in app/serializers.py.
- analytics/: Streamlit admin analytics. Calculations only in ayana_analytics/metrics.py (pure pandas, tested);
  pages in pages/; colours and filters in ayana_analytics/ui.py.
- Money is always integer paise in the database. Prices are computed on the server, never trusted from the client.
- JSON sent to the website uses camelCase keys; Python code and database columns use snake_case.
- After changing api/app/models.py: `alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<what>"` then `alembic upgrade head` (inside api/).
- Run tests before committing: `cd api && pytest`, `cd analytics && pytest`.
- Docs live in docs/. Keep docs/04-api.md and docs/11-streamlit-analytics.md in sync when adding endpoints or metrics.
